  "report_period": "Week 50 (9th Dec to 16th Dec 2022)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Hokoku Marine have committed their Kamsarmax \"Nord Pollux\" 81/2016 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 01/2026, DD 12/2023, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for low USD 25 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Lowlands Comfort\" 81/2016 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 02/2026, DD 02/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 26,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Eagle Bulk Shipping sold their \"Jaeger\" 52/2004 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 10/2024, DD 01/2023, BWTS fitted) to Middle Eastern buyers for USD 10,5 mill, while the sister vessel \"Worldera-5\" 52/2004 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS/DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at low USD 10 mill. Following the sale of the \"Interlink Activity\" 38/2015 Taizhou, China (SS 09/2025, DD 07/2023, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) at USD 21 mill, Mssrs Ocean Yield have now committed the sister vessel \"Interlink Sagacity\" 38/2015 Taizhou, China (SS 08/2025, DD 08/2023, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) to undisclosed buyers for USD 20 mill. Moreover, Anthony Giavridis Maritime sold their \"Gant Grace\" 28/2010 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for USD 12,5 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Melina\" 28/2009 Imabari, Japan (SS 08/2024, DD overdue) was sold basis DD passed & BWTS fitted at USD 10,9 mill.",
    "tankers": "Ridgebury Holdings have committed their Suezmax \"Ridgebury Mary Jane\" 150/2008 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 05/2023, Scrubber fitted) to undisclosed buyers for USD 38,5 mill. Remind you that a month ago, same owners sold the one-year-older \"Ridgebury Nicholas A\" 159/2007 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 01/2023, Scrubber fitted) at USD 34 mill. The LR1 \"Summit Africa\" 73/2009 New Times, China (SS/DD 08/2024) was sold to European buyers for mid-high USD 24 mill. Note that back in November, the \"Cape Tampa\" 73/2009 New Times, China (SS/DD 03/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 20,25 mill. Stealth Maritime have committed their MR2 \"T Rex\" 50/2006 Spp, Korea (SS 12/2026, DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) for USD 19,2 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger \"Clean Imperial\" 50/2007 Sls, Korea (SS/DD 11/2022) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 20 mill basis SS/DD passed & BWTS fitted.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid usd 8,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 10,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 12,000/15,000 pd. Southeast Asian trips via East Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via South America were fixed around 20,000/22,000 pd. Continental trips via US Gulf into China were reported at the level of usd 25,000/28,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 32,000 pd. A Kamsarmax was reported fixed on a period at the level of usd 16,000 pd for 11/14 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips into East Coast India with fertilizers were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into East Coast India were fixed around usd 12,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd. An Ultramax was reported fixed on a period at the level of usd 13,850 pd for 10/12 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of trips from China into India with petcoke were reported at the level of usd 8,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 21,000 pd. South America Coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 18,000/21,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
